@startuml d9-plugins
title D9 - Configured Go plugins; asynchronous derived-data feedback
rectangle "mkts.yml\n(default plugin examples are commented)" as cfg
rectangle "plugins.Load(name)\nplugin.Open from GOPATH/bin or ./\n(plugins/load.go:44)" as load
rectangle "Trigger plugin\nNewTrigger(config) -> Fire(keyPath, records)\ne.g. ondiskagg: 1Min -> 5Min/1H/1D bars" as trig
rectangle "BgWorker plugin\nNewBgWorker(config) -> Run()\ne.g. alpacabkfeeder, polygon, iex" as bg
rectangle "TriggerPluginDispatcher\nmatch 'on' pattern, fire in goroutine,\nrecover panics (written.go)" as disp
rectangle "Writer.WriteCSM" as w
rectangle "QueryService.ExecuteQuery\nplanner + Reader (base data)" as q
cfg --> load : triggers: module/on/config\nbgworkers: module/name/config
load --> trig
load --> bg
w --> disp : normal flush records; may include primary-write errors
disp --> trig : Fire asynchronously
bg --> w : write fetched market data
trig --> q : ondiskagg reads base bars
trig --> w : ondiskagg writes derived bars
note bottom of disp
  Select base-data patterns to avoid unwanted feedback.
  Derived updates may lag Write responses.
  Crash-WAL replay writes primary data directly:
  aggregation/stream triggers are not rerun.
  Replica apply uses WriteCSM: replica triggers run.
end note
note bottom of load
  Go plugin.Open; plugins built with -buildmode=plugin.
  Load test runs only on Linux (plugins/load_test.go).
  contrib READMEs name Linux and macOS.
  WSL is one Linux option.
end note
@enduml
